                <pb facs="0693" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg565"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 407.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bingham to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokio, Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 9, 1885</date>.
                        (Received July 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2064.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 2056, dated the 30th
                    ultimo, wherewith I had the honor to inclose a copy of my note to his excellency
                    Count Inouye, dated the 29th ultimo, conveying, in pursuance of your
                    instruction, an expression of the thanks of our Government to that of Japan for
                    the timely service rendered by His Majesty’s troops at Seoul in February last, I
                    now have the pleasure to inclose herewith a translated copy of Count Inouye’s
                    reply thereto, dated the 8th instant.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JNO. A. BINGHAM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
